1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:03,815
This saber-toothed cub
is over 35,000 years old.

2
00:00:04,318 --> 00:00:06,268
And its fur
is still here.

3
00:00:06,749 --> 00:00:08,604
Found in Siberian permafrost,

4
00:00:09,082 --> 00:00:10,716
these are preserved remains,

5
00:00:11,197 --> 00:00:12,436
not a living animal.

6
00:00:12,932 --> 00:00:15,589
Scientists studied
its skull and teeth

7
00:00:15,901 --> 00:00:17,285
using CT imaging.

8
00:00:17,735 --> 00:00:20,097
The animal was Homotherium,

9
00:00:20,535 --> 00:00:22,755
an extinct saber-toothed cat.

10
00:00:23,195 --> 00:00:26,913
Its tooth development suggests
it was only about three weeks old.

11
00:00:27,379 --> 00:00:29,621
Compared with a
similar-aged lion cub,

12
00:00:30,070 --> 00:00:31,338
it had smaller ears,

13
00:00:31,661 --> 00:00:32,522
a powerful neck,

14
00:00:32,832 --> 00:00:34,260
and broader front paws.

15
00:00:34,728 --> 00:00:38,546
Those soft-tissue details are things
a bare skeleton cannot show.

16
00:00:39,045 --> 00:00:40,542
But the mummy is incomplete.

17
00:00:41,040 --> 00:00:43,574
A full living appearance
still needs reconstruction.

18
00:00:44,053 --> 00:00:45,278
Not a resurrected predator.

19
00:00:45,709 --> 00:00:47,636
A tiny survivor of deep time,

20
00:00:48,142 --> 00:00:50,073
revealing what bones alone
leave out.
